Visual Design Spec — "Enrichment Rule Propagation" Diagram
(Extracted from Confluence reference screenshots, for exact visual replication)
1. Overall Page Structure
Top banner: full-width horizontal bar, dark teal/slate fill, spans entire page width. Contains the diagram title only ("Enrichment Rule Propagation"), left-aligned, bold white text, ~16-18px.
Section labels are on the LEFT edge, not as horizontal headers per section. Each major section (lane) has a narrow vertical strip (~40-50px wide) running along the far-left edge of that section's row-band, filled dark teal/slate, with the section name as white text rotated 90° (reading bottom-to-top).
Sections: "Payment Enrichment UI - UT Environment", "Migrate Feature Branch Scripts to Develop and Main", "Rule Propagation flow GPP SIT/UAT and PROD"
Sub-labels within a section (e.g. "UT Environment", "SIT/UAT/OAT", "PROD") are plain text, small, teal/blue-gray color, top-left of that sub-block — not boxed or colored as a bar.
Canvas background: white / very light gray, faint grid visible (like graph paper), very subtle — not a strong visual element.
Right edge: a single shared Git Repository icon, positioned far right, roughly vertically centered across the whole diagram height. Multiple thin vertical/orthogonal lines converge into it from different sections (acts like a shared "bus").
Flow direction: strictly left → right within each section; sections stack top → bottom in chronological order (UT → Git merge → SIT/UAT/OAT → PROD).
Numbered arrows: every arrow has a small black number/label near it (1, 2, 3, 3.1, 6. Fail, 11. Yes, etc.) indicating sequence.
