4. Typography
Sans-serif throughout (looks like Arial/Helvetica/Calibri).
Titles/banners: bold, white, ~16-18px.
Box labels: regular weight, black, ~11-12px, centered.
Arrow/step numbers: smaller, ~9-10px, positioned just above or beside the line.
Sticky note text: ~9-10px, left-aligned (not centered), slightly condensed.
5. Layout & Spacing Conventions
Consistent vertical alignment: actor icons sit in a fixed left-hand column across all rows within a section (e.g., all "Maker"/"Checker" icons align to the same x-position).
Generous horizontal spacing between boxes (~80-120px gaps) so arrows never need to double back through other shapes.
Decision diamonds are noticeably larger than process rectangles to draw the eye.
Loop-back arrows (e.g., "Fail", "No") route above or below the main flow line, never crossing directly through other boxes.
Each section is a full-width horizontal band; the Git Repository connector lines run down the far-right margin only, never crossing into the middle of the canvas.
No dashed lines anywhere — every connector in the original is solid.
6. Suggested prompt block to hand another AI/tool
Recreate this diagram using: a dark teal (#2C4A4A) title banner across the top; vertical rotated-text section labels in the same dark teal running down the left margin (not horizontal headers per section); light gray rounded rectangles with subtle drop-shadow for all process steps; dark teal diamonds with white bold text for decisions; green gradient 3D cylinders for databases; blue double-cylinder-plus-lightning-bolt icons for Hazelcast/cache; a black diamond with a white git-fork glyph for the shared Git Repository node on the far right; flat gradient teal-green person-silhouette icons (not UML stick figures) for human actors; cream/yellow folded-corner sticky notes for annotations; solid black arrows with small numbered labels; generous spacing so no line crosses through another shape.